@page "/components/copybutton"
@page "/components/copy-button"

<PageOutlet Url="components/copybutton"
            Title="CopyButton"
            Description="BitCopyButton puts a value on the clipboard and confirms it: for a moment its glyph turns into a check mark, its text says so, and the copy is announced to screen readers." />

<DemoPage Name="CopyButton"
          SecondaryNames="@(["ClipboardButton", "CopyToClipboardButton"])"
          Description="BitCopyButton puts a value on the clipboard and confirms it, because a copy button that gives no feedback leaves the user guessing whether it worked: for CopiedDuration after the copy its glyph is a check mark, its text says Copied, and a polite live region announces it. It is a BitButton, with the button's variants, sizes and colors, an icon button when it is given no Text, and is disabled while it has no Value."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          SubEnums="componentSubEnums"
          GitHubExtrasUrl="CopyButton/BitCopyButton.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="Extras/CopyButton/BitCopyButtonDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.Extras" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.Extras"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The button needs no service. It writes through the Clipboard API of the browser, which only works in a secure context
            (https, or localhost); elsewhere, and where the browser refuses it, it falls back to the copy command of the page. It
            only confirms a copy that happened: one that still fails confirms nothing (taking off a confirmation still showing)
            and raises OnCopyFailed. Its
            default texts (Copy, Copied) come from <b>BitStrings</b>, which translates them for the whole app.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                Give it the <b>Value</b> to copy. Without a <b>Text</b> it is an icon button named Copy. Press it: for two seconds
                the glyph is a check mark and its name says Copied, and a screen reader hears it.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <code>dotnet add package Bit.BlazorUI.Extras</code>
                <BitCopyButton Value="dotnet add package Bit.BlazorUI.Extras" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Text & CopiedText" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Text</b> shows a text beside the icon, and <b>CopiedText</b> takes its place while the copy is confirmed
                (Copied by default). The live region announces the copied text too. Without a Text, <b>AriaLabel</b> names
                the icon button (and is its tooltip) in place of Copy.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="https://blazorui.bitplatform.dev" Text="Copy" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="https://blazorui.bitplatform.dev" Text="Copy link" CopiedText="Link copied!" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="https://blazorui.bitplatform.dev" AriaLabel="Copy link" CopiedText="Link copied!" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Icons" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>IconName</b> replaces the Copy glyph, and <b>CopiedIconName</b> the check mark the button shows once it copied.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="https://blazorui.bitplatform.dev" IconName="@BitIconName.Link" Text="Copy link" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="https://blazorui.bitplatform.dev"
                               IconName="@BitIconName.Share"
                               CopiedIconName="@BitIconName.CompletedSolid"
                               Text="Share"
                               CopiedText="Ready to paste" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Variant" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4">
            <div>The button's three variants: Fill (the default), Outline and Text.</div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="Fill" Text="Fill" Variant="BitVariant.Fill" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Outline" Text="Outline" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Text" Text="Text" Variant="BitVariant.Text" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Fill" Variant="BitVariant.Fill" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Outline" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Text" Variant="BitVariant.Text" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="CopiedDuration & OnCopy" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>CopiedDuration</b> is how long the copied state stays on the button (two seconds by default); a copy while it
                is showing starts it over. <b>OnCopy</b> is raised with the value once it is on the clipboard, and
                <b>OnCopyFailed</b> with the error when the browser could not put it there - never both.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="An answer worth keeping."
                               Text="Copy"
                               CopiedDuration="TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)"
                               OnCopy="HandleCopy"
                               OnCopyFailed="HandleCopyFailed" />
                <span>Copied @copyCount time(s)@(copyError is null ? null : $", last error: {copyError}")</span>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Value" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                <b>Value</b> is read when the button is pressed, so it can follow what changes - here what is typed. While it is
                null the button is disabled: here until something is typed. An empty text that is given as such
                (<b>Value=""</b>) is still copied.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitTextField @bind-Value="draft" Immediate Placeholder="Type something to copy" Style="flex:1" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="@draft" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" Id="example7">
            <div>
                A <b>Disabled</b> copy button copies nothing, whoever presses it - the click a screen reader or a script still
                delivers to a disabled button included - and raises no <b>OnCopy</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Disabled Value="Nothing to see here" />
                <BitCopyButton Disabled Value="Nothing to see here" Text="Copy" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitCopyButtonParams</b> sets the look, the texts and the <b>CopiedDuration</b> of every
                copy button inside it; a parameter of the button itself still wins (the third has its own variant).
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitParams Parameters="copyButtonParams">
                <div class="example-content">
                    <BitCopyButton Value="First snippet" />
                    <BitCopyButton Value="Second snippet" />
                    <BitCopyButton Value="Third snippet" Variant="BitVariant.Fill" />
                </div>
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Color" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" Id="example9">
            <div>The button's general colors, Primary being the default.</div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="Primary" Text="Primary" Color="BitColor.Primary" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Secondary" Text="Secondary" Color="BitColor.Secondary" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Tertiary" Text="Tertiary" Color="BitColor.Tertiary" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Info" Text="Info" Color="BitColor.Info" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Success" Text="Success" Color="BitColor.Success" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Warning" Text="Warning" Color="BitColor.Warning" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="SevereWarning" Text="SevereWarning" Color="BitColor.SevereWarning" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Error" Text="Error" Color="BitColor.Error" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="External Icons" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" Id="example10">
            <div>
                The built-in icon set is not a requirement. <b>Icon</b> and <b>CopiedIcon</b> take a <b>BitIconInfo</b> that
                renders whatever CSS classes you give it, so any icon font works - <b>BitIconInfo.Fa</b> for FontAwesome,
                <b>BitIconInfo.Bi</b> for Bootstrap Icons, or <b>BitIconInfo.Css</b> for anything else. Just remember to
                reference the library's stylesheet yourself.
            </div>
            <br />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/7.0.1/css/all.min.css" />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css" />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="FontAwesome"
                               Text="FontAwesome"
                               Icon="@BitIconInfo.Fa("regular copy")"
                               CopiedIcon="@BitIconInfo.Fa("solid check")" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Bootstrap Icons"
                               Text="Bootstrap Icons"
                               Icon="@BitIconInfo.Bi("clipboard")"
                               CopiedIcon="@BitIconInfo.Bi("clipboard-check")" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Size" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" Id="example11">
            <div>The button's three sizes: Small, Medium (the default) and Large.</div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="Small" Text="Small" Size="BitSize.Small" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Medium" Text="Medium" Size="BitSize.Medium" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Large" Text="Large" Size="BitSize.Large" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Small" Size="BitSize.Small" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Medium" Size="BitSize.Medium" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Large" Size="BitSize.Large" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example12RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example12CsharpCode" Id="example12">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> and <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> and <b>Classes</b> its button (BitButtonClassStyles) and
                its visually hidden live region. The copy button has no CSS variables of its own: the button is a BitButton,
                restyled through the public <b>--bit-Button-*</b> variables, from <b>:root</b>, an ancestor or <b>Style</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Value="Styled" Style="border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri);border-radius:0.5rem;padding:0.25rem" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Classy" Class="custom-class" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Styles" Text="Styles" Styles="@(new() { Button = new() { Root = "border-radius:2rem", Icon = "color:var(--bit-clr-sec)" } })" />
                <BitCopyButton Value="Classes" Text="Classes" Classes="@(new() { Button = new() { Root = "custom-button" } })" />
                <span style="@cssVariablesStyle">
                    <BitCopyButton Value="Variables" Text="Variables" />
                </span>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example13RazorCode" Id="example13">
            <div>Use BitCopyButton in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl" class="example-content">
                <BitCopyButton Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Value="سلام دنیا" Text="کپی" CopiedText="کپی شد" />
                <BitCopyButton Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Value="سلام دنیا" AriaLabel="کپی" CopiedText="کپی شد" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
